:name: WS500 stock-firmware peripheral trace
:description: Boots the STOCK WS500 image and logs RCC/TIM1/ADC/I2C accesses (PROJECT_PLAN §0.6 V6).

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DIAGNOSTIC / BONUS script — NOT part of CI.
#
# Purpose: dynamic corroboration of the static binary RE (V1-V3, V7). Booting
# the real stock image under Renode and logging peripheral bus traffic lets us
# watch TIM1 (field PWM) configuration, the ADC scan setup, and I2C traffic to
# 0x40 (INA226) / 0x50 (EEPROM) as they actually happen.
#
# The stock image is proprietary and is NOT committed to this repo. Either drop
# a copy at the space-free default path below (build/fw_stock_0x08000000.bin) or
# override $bin on the command line. Quote the path if it contains spaces (the
# Monitor splits on whitespace), e.g.:
#   renode -e "$bin=@'../New folder/fw_0x08000000.bin'; include @renode/ws500-stock-trace.resc"
#
# NOTE: the stock firmware may stall once it hits a peripheral behaviour Renode
# doesn't model (most likely HSI48RDY in RCC — the stock code, unlike ours,
# probably checks the HAL return). That's fine: the RCC/TIM1/ADC/I2C access log
# captured up to that point is the artefact we want. This script traces, it
# does not assert liveness.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Space-free default drop location (see note above); override with $bin.
$bin?=@build/fw_stock_0x08000000.bin

using sysbus

mach create "ws500-stock"
machine LoadPlatformDescription @renode/ws500f072.repl

# Raw binary (no ELF metadata): map it at the flash base...
sysbus LoadBinary $bin 0x08000000
# ...and boot Cortex-M from the vector table there (initial SP @ +0x0, PC @ +0x4).
sysbus.cpu VectorTableOffset 0x08000000
sysbus.cpu SP `sysbus ReadDoubleWord 0x08000000`
sysbus.cpu PC `sysbus ReadDoubleWord 0x08000004`

# Trace the peripherals that carry the V1-V3/V7 evidence.
sysbus LogPeripheralAccess sysbus.rcc true
sysbus LogPeripheralAccess sysbus.timer1 true
sysbus LogPeripheralAccess sysbus.adc true
sysbus LogPeripheralAccess sysbus.i2c1 true
sysbus LogPeripheralAccess sysbus.i2c2 true

# Make the access logs visible.
logLevel 0

# Run a bounded slice, then inspect the log / `sysbus.cpu PC`.
start
